WEBVTT

NOTE station-details: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.038
Some stations drive
more than one sprinkler.

V0-2
00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:08.000
Expand the row to see what
each head actually measured.

V1a-1
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:15.502
A chevron beside the
station name means the

V1a-2
00:00:15.602 --> 00:00:18.100
station has more than one
sprinkler paired to it.

V1b-1
00:00:20.127 --> 00:00:22.887
Without the chevron,
the row is the whole story.

V2a-1
00:00:28.997 --> 00:00:32.098
Each child row is named for
its parent and numbered,

V2a-2
00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:35.777
and carries its own scan date
and its own measured moisture.

V2b-1
00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:40.458
Nothing else is editable
at sprinkler level.

V2b-2
00:00:40.558 --> 00:00:43.310
The target and the adjustment
belong to the station.

V3a-1
00:00:50.603 --> 00:00:53.943
The station's average VWC is
the mean of its sprinklers.

V3b-1
00:00:56.270 --> 00:01:01.023
Two heads reading 31.4 and 30.4
give a station average of 30.9,

V3b-2
00:01:01.123 --> 00:01:05.500
and a station that looks fine
can still hide one dry head.

V4a-1
00:01:12.417 --> 00:01:15.162
A child whose scan is
older than today shows a

V4a-2
00:01:15.262 --> 00:01:18.425
modelled value marked with
an orange calculator icon,

V4a-3
00:01:18.525 --> 00:01:22.287
and the parent average is then
part measurement and part model.

V4b-1
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.058
The parent row carries a grey
calculator icon beside its average,

V4b-2
00:01:28.158 --> 00:01:30.660
so you can tell it includes
a modelled reading.
